#### Polymorphism
--------UPCASTING---------
-- upcasting is a features in java where a child class object is stored  in parent class refrence.
-- this happens automatically and is part of java inheritence system
 **  Why we use it.
    --  to treat multiple type as one
    --  to write cleanes and reusable code.
    --  to allow java to decide behaviour at runtime.

Q. IS upcasting done implicitly or explicitly in java?
  -- Upcasting is done implicitly in java since the subclass object is types of a its super class.
     e.g:- my friend went to a resturant and ordered a pizza but instead of saying pizza he just told bring me a food. waiter will serve a general food --> food  ---> what he actually gets a pizza.

